1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:05,266
Every day, sunlight lands on your roof.

2
00:00:05,426 --> 00:00:07,356
Most of it turns into heat and

3
00:00:07,356 --> 00:00:12,773
drifts away. A solar panel catches that

4
00:00:12,773 --> 00:00:14,667
light and turns part of it into

5
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:19,855
electricity.

6
00:00:20,428 --> 00:00:25,488
Inside the panel sit many silicon cells.

7
00:00:25,648 --> 00:00:28,752
When light particles, called photons, hit the

8
00:00:28,752 --> 00:00:36,441
silicon, they knock electrons loose.

9
00:00:37,012 --> 00:00:39,903
The panel produces direct current, which always

10
00:00:39,903 --> 00:00:46,574
flows one way. Your home needs alternating

11
00:00:46,574 --> 00:00:49,137
current that changes direction many times a

12
00:00:49,137 --> 00:00:57,951
second. An inverter makes that change.

13
00:00:58,512 --> 00:01:01,742
Light in, electrons moving, an inverter shaping

14
00:01:01,742 --> 00:01:04,205
the current, and a battery holding it:

15
00:01:04,205 --> 00:01:05,937
that is how a solar panel powers

16
00:01:05,937 --> 00:01:14,439
a home.
